WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.103
In 1949, the People's Republic of China was founded in Beijing.

00:00:05.103 --> 00:00:09.096
The square was packed with crowds welcoming a new era.

00:00:09.096 --> 00:00:13.083
The new capital also began new construction.

00:00:13.083 --> 00:00:16.143
At the same time, the Republic of China government moved to Taiwan.

00:00:16.143 --> 00:00:20.107
Many people crossed the sea by boat to an unfamiliar island.

00:00:20.107 --> 00:00:23.114
The docks were crowded with people saying goodbye.

00:00:23.114 --> 00:00:27.083
Ships arrived in Taiwan as the coast drew closer.

00:00:27.083 --> 00:00:30.125
People brought their luggage and began a new life.

00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:34.083
From then on, the two sides were ruled by different governments.

00:00:34.083 --> 00:00:38.068
A strait separated many family members.

00:00:38.068 --> 00:00:41.125
Waves beat against the shores on both sides day and night.

00:00:41.125 --> 00:00:44.135
Family members could only share their longing through letters.

00:00:44.135 --> 00:00:48.096
Many stories from then on had different endings.

00:00:48.096 --> 00:00:52.068
Letter after letter from home came across the ocean.

00:00:52.068 --> 00:00:55.125
Cross-strait relations are complex and intertwined.

00:00:55.125 --> 00:00:58.547
This history continues to have an impact to this day.
